    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d395">

                <pb facs="0530" n="462" sameAs="frus:frus1867p1/pg462"/>

                <head>Mr. G. F. Seward to Mr.
                        Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 225.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">United States Consulate General</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">Shanghai</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-12-11"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 11, 1866</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my despatch No. 188, I have
                    now the honor to forward to you a copy of a despatch which I have just addressed
                    to the minister, in the same matter, viz: the expulsion of American merchants
                    from the north bank of the Yangtsi at Chinkiang, together with copies of a
                    despatch from the Tantai at that port, dated October 8, and my response of the
                    13th of the same month; which deal with various points involved.</p>
                <p>I have the honor, <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c</hi>.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GEO. F. SEWARD.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
